SUMMARY:Elementary Educator Ceramics Workshop
DESCRIPTION:If you’re an elementary school teacher and have been wanting to introduce clay projects in your classroom\, this three-day workshop is for you! Build your understanding of ceramics and gain the confidence to lead engaging clay projects with your students. In a supportive environment\, you’ll learn kid-friendly projects that can be completed in a single day or over multiple weeks\, and you’ll receive hands-on guidance in loading and firing a kiln. Connect with a creative community of fellow elementary school teachers and leave with practical skills and project ideas you can bring directly into your classroom!\n● Day 1: One-day and weekly projects\n● Day 2: Underglazing\, textures & loading a bisque kiln\n● Day 3: Glazing & loading a glaze kiln\nInstructor: Vex Rios (They/Them/Theirs)\nAGES 18+\nPrice: $150\nTime: Tuesdays\, 5:30-8:00 pm\nWorkshop date:\nJuly 14-July 28
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/elementary-educator-ceramics-workshop/2026-07-21/
LOCATION:Davis Arts Center\, 1919 F St\, Davis\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Elementary-Educator-Ceramics-Workshop.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Davis Arts Center":MAILTO:office@davisartscenter.org
END:VEVENT
